/T (AI uses neural networks, which are computer programs made of layers of mathematical nodes to learn datasets and patterns of proteins. Nodes convert an input given by us to numbers so computers can understand. Then, by stacking multiple layers of protein, AI learns to predict the 3D shape of a protein it will fold into. After this process, it will test each shape over and over while improving until it concludes. But how does making a 3D shape of a protein help in cancer?)
