1191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Veda Sharma, 11: Every day, nearly 60 million stray dogs roam Indian streets. For some, they are cute, loyal, and friendly companions, while for others, they are a daily threat. But the dogs are not the question here; it's about who takes responsibility.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Supreme Court has been drawn into this debate after cases of dog bites and rabies deaths. Residents approach the Court demanding protection and stricter control over stray dog populations, demanding safety from this menace. On the other hand, NGOs, activists, and animal rights groups criticise and oppose the Supreme Court ruling on the relocation of stray dogs as unfeasible and argue that dogs too have a constitutional right to life and compassion under Article 51A\(g\). )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11 12]
>>
endobj
1193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This crisis is not really about dogs; it's about governance. By relying on the Supreme Court to settle what should be addressed in local governments and state parliaments, India shows its inability to balance public safety with animal welfare. Unless political leaders and institutions step up with a clear, humane, and enforceable national strategy, the problem will only grow.)
/Pg 19 0 R
>>
endobj
